# Quickstart

## MCP for Aura

Before connecting, enable Tool authentication in Security for your organization in the Aura console. See Enable tool authentication for details.

First, retrieve your instance’s MCP server URL:

  1. Under Instances in the left side navigation of the Aura Console, retrieve the ID of the Aura instance you would like to use with Neo4j MCP.

  2. Substitute the ID in the following template to get your MCP server URL: `https://<INSTANCE_ID>.mcp-instances.neo4j.io`.

For a visual walkthrough, or to copy the URL directly from the instance details, see Find your MCP server URL.

Then add Neo4j MCP to your client’s MCP configuration. For example, in VS Code, create or edit `mcp.json`:

    `{
      "servers": {
        "neo4j-mcp": {
          "type": "http",
          "url": "https://<instance-id>.mcp-instances.neo4j.io"
        }
      }
    }`

See Client configuration for other client-specific configuration.

## Self hosted

Install uv to make `uvx` available on your PATH.

Add Neo4j MCP to your client’s MCP configuration. For example, in VS Code, create or edit `mcp.json`:

    `{
      "servers": {
        "neo4j": {
          "type": "stdio",
          "command": "uvx",
          "args": ["neo4j-mcp-server"],
          "env": {
            "NEO4J_MCP_URI": "bolt://localhost:7687",
            "NEO4J_MCP_USERNAME": "neo4j",
            "NEO4J_MCP_PASSWORD": "password",
            "NEO4J_MCP_DATABASE": "neo4j",
            "NEO4J_MCP_READ_ONLY": "true",
            "NEO4J_MCP_TELEMETRY": "false",
            "NEO4J_MCP_LOG_LEVEL": "info",
            "NEO4J_MCP_LOG_FORMAT": "text",
            "NEO4J_MCP_SCHEMA_SAMPLE_SIZE": "100"
          }
        }
      }
    }`

See Client configuration f

